problem:
Problem description
- There is a factory that produces a set of products $$\mathcal{P}$$ over a planning horizon $$\mathcal{T}$$ using a set of shared production processes $$\mathcal{R}$$.
- Each product $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$ requires a known amount of processing time on each process $$r \in \mathcal{R}$$, represented by the parameter $$a_{r,p}$$.
- Each product $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$ generates a unit profit $$\pi_{p,t}$$ in period $$t \in \mathcal{T}$$.
- Each process $$r \in \mathcal{R}$$ has a regular available capacity $$c_{r,t}$$ in each period $$t \in \mathcal{T}$$.
- Some processes may also allow overtime, with overtime availability or limit represented by the parameter $$\Omega_{r,t}$$ when applicable.
- The planning goal is to maximize total profit over the horizon while respecting production requirements and process utilization goals.
- The total production of each product must meet or exceed its minimum required level $$\ell_{p,t}$$ in each period $$t \in \mathcal{T}$$.
- The overall profit in each period must meet or exceed the target profit level $$G_t$$.
- The operating time assigned to Process $$\mathrm{I}$$ must match its required target utilization $$H_{\mathrm{I},t}$$ exactly in each period $$t \in \mathcal{T}$$.
- Process $$\mathrm{II}$$ must be fully utilized at its regular capacity, and overtime may be used if needed and permitted for that process.
- Production decisions must be feasible with respect to the available process times, and the processing time consumed by each product must be consistent with the product mix selected.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_{p,t}$$: quantity of product $$p$$ produced in period $$t$$.
  - $$u_{r,t}$$: regular hours assigned to process $$r$$ in period $$t$$.
  - $$o_{r,t}$$: overtime hours assigned to process $$r$$ in period $$t$$, if overtime is allowed.
  - Optional deviation variables for target shortfalls or excesses, if a goal-programming representation is used, such as deviations for profit, production minimums, and exact process utilization.

Input Format
{
  "products": "List of product identifiers, size $$P = |\\mathcal{P}|$$.",
  "processes": "List of process identifiers, size $$R = |\\mathcal{R}|$$.",
  "periods": "List of planning periods, size $$T = |\\mathcal{T}|$$.",
  "processing_time": "Matrix $$a_{r,p}$$ of size $$R \\times P$$, where $$a_{r,p}$$ is the hours required on process $$r$$ for one unit of product $$p$$.",
  "unit_profit": "Matrix or vector $$\\pi_{p,t}$$ of size $$P \\times T$$, where $$\\pi_{p,t}$$ is the profit per unit of product $$p$$ in period $$t$$.",
  "regular_capacity": "Matrix $$c_{r,t}$$ of size $$R \\times T$$, where $$c_{r,t}$$ is the regular available hours of process $$r$$ in period $$t$$.",
  "minimum_production": "Matrix $$\\ell_{p,t}$$ of size $$P \\times T$$, where $$\\ell_{p,t}$$ is the minimum required production of product $$p$$ in period $$t$$.",
  "profit_target": "Vector $$G_t$$ of size $$T$$, where $$G_t$$ is the minimum required total profit in period $$t$$.",
  "process_time_target": "Matrix $$H_{r,t}$$ of size $$R \\times T$$, where $$H_{r,t}$$ is the required utilization target for process $$r$$ in period $$t$$.",
  "overtime_allowed": "Matrix of logical flags or limits $$\\Omega_{r,t}$$ indicating whether overtime is allowed for process $$r$$ in period $$t$$ and, if relevant, the maximum overtime available.",
  "objective": "Maximize total profit over the planning horizon while satisfying the stated production and utilization requirements."
}

Output Format
{
  "production_plan": "Matrix $$x_{p,t}$$ of size $$P \\times T$$, where $$x_{p,t}$$ is the production quantity of product $$p$$ in period $$t$$.",
  "regular_process_usage": "Matrix $$u_{r,t}$$ of size $$R \\times T$$, where $$u_{r,t}$$ is the regular time used on process $$r$$ in period $$t$$.",
  "overtime_plan": "Matrix $$o_{r,t}$$ of size $$R \\times T$$, where $$o_{r,t}$$ is the overtime time used on process $$r$$ in period $$t$$, if overtime is allowed.",
  "goal_deviations": "Optional structured record of deviations from target profit and process utilization goals, if the model uses deviation variables.",
  "total_profit": "Scalar value giving the achieved total profit over the planning horizon."
}

